### National CanSat Competition

The National CanSat Competition provides Sri Lankan students with their first end-to-end hands-on experience in space systems engineering. A CanSat is a simulation of a real satellite, integrated within the volume and shape of a regular soft drinks can.

### Mission Objectives

- **Primary Mission**: Atmospheric sounding, telemetry transmission, and safe descent velocity control under parachute.
- **Secondary Science Mission**: Air quality gas detection, high-resolution camera imaging, target landing trajectory guidance, or environmental radiation measurement.
- **Launch & Recovery**: CanSats are deployed from drones or weather balloons at altitudes up to 500 meters, transmitting real-time telemetry back to student ground stations.
